From 092928372eb6ca383facd595575906cb1b6b8d70 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cindy Krafft <cynthiacondra@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 00:39:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix k-mer heuristic missing anchored adapters with an
 inserted base

The k-mer search sets for the partial-overlap classes of an adapter use a
window that is exactly as long as the longest adapter prefix of the class.
An occurrence of that prefix with insertions in the read spans up to
max_errors more positions, so the k-mer chunk on the far side of the
insertion lies outside the window and kmers_present() returns False even
though the aligner accepts the occurrence. Regular 3'/5' adapters were
covered by their internal search set, but anchored and non-internal
adapters have no such set and lost about 40 % of the reads with one inserted
base whenever exactly one error was allowed (two chunks).

Extend each window by the number of allowed errors of its class.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TaHntBDKuZJpMAAMenkC44
